    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3327" root="بندق" body-key="b">
    
      Q. 1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَنْدَقَ</span></b>  <i>He made</i> a thing <i>into</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَنَادِق</span> [meaning <i>bullets,</i> or <i>little balls</i>], (Mgh, K,) or <i>like</i>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بنادق</span> (TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  [In post-classical Arabic, <i>He
shot a bullet,</i> or <i>bullets,</i> from a cross-bow or
other weapon.] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بندق إِلَيْهِ</span> (assumed tropical:)  <i>He looked sharply,</i>
or <i>intently, at him,</i> or <i>it.</i> (Ibn-'Abbád, K.)

